            "output": "<path>/Users/aasheesh/Documents/webdev/os/cli/docs/architecture/agent-integration-checklist.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Agent Integration Checklist\n2: \n3: This document provides requirements and a checklist for integrating new AI coding agents with Entire. Use this to validate your implementation is correct and complete.\n4: \n5: For step-by-step implementation instructions, code templates, and testing patterns, see the [Agent Implementation Guide](agent-guide.md).\n6: \n7: ## Core Principle: Full Transcript Storage\n8: \n9: Entire stores the **complete session transcript** at every checkpoint, not incremental diffs. This enables:\n10: \n11: - Simple rewind: restore the full transcript, agent resumes from that state\n12: - No dependency on previous checkpoints being intact\n13: - Consistent behavior across all checkpoint types (committed, uncommitted)\n14: \n15: **Each checkpoint must contain the full session history up to that point.**\n16: \n17: ## Core Principle: Native Format Preservation\n18: \n19: Store transcripts in the **agent's native format**. Any transformation or normalization should only be done to support CLI features (rewind, resume, summarization, file extraction), not for backend or web UI consumption.\n20: \n21: **Why:**\n22: - The backend/web UI should handle format differences, not the CLI\n23: - Transforming for downstream consumers couples the CLI to their requirements\n24: - Native formats ensure compatibility with agent's own import/export tools\n25: - Reduces risk of data loss from lossy transformations\n26: - Format changes that break the UI can be fixed with a backend deploy; CLI changes require a full release cycle and user adoption\n27: \n28: **Do:**\n29: - Store the raw transcript as the agent produces it\n30: - Parse the native format when CLI features need specific data (e.g., extract file paths for `entire status`)\n31: - Let the backend normalize formats for display\n32: \n33: **Don't:**\n34: - Create a \"universal transcript format\" in the CLI\n35: - Transform logs to match what the web UI expects\n36: - Strip or restructure data to simplify backend processing\n37: - Create intermediate formats (e.g., converting JSON to JSONL for \"easier parsing\")\n38: - Reconstruct transcripts from events when a canonical export exists\n39: \n40: ## Integration Checklist\n41: \n42: ### Transcript Capture\n43: \n44: See Guide: [Transcript Format Guide](agent-guide.md#transcript-format-guide), [TranscriptAnalyzer](agent-guide.md#transcriptanalyzer), [TranscriptPreparer](agent-guide.md#transcriptpreparer)\n45: \n46: - [ ] **Full transcript on every turn**: At turn-end, capture the complete session transcript, not just events since the last checkpoint\n47: - [ ] **Resumed session handling**: When a user resumes an existing session, the transcript must include all historical messages, not just new ones since the plugin/hook loaded\n48: - [ ] **Use agent's canonical export**: Prefer the agent's native export command (e.g., reading Claude's JSONL file, Gemini's JSON, Cursor's JSONL, Factory AI Droid's JSONL, Copilot CLI's JSONL, OpenCode's `opencode export` JSON) over manually reconstructing from events\n49: - [ ] **No custom formats**: Store the agent's native format directly in `NativeData` - do not convert between formats (e.g., JSON to JSONL) or create intermediate representations\n50: - [ ] **Graceful degradation**: If the canonical source is unavailable (e.g., agent shutting down), fall back to best-effort capture with clear documentation of limitations\n51: \n52: ### Session Storage Abstraction\n53: \n54: See Guide: [Step 3 - Core Agent Interface](agent-guide.md#step-3-implement-core-agent-interface-youragentgo)\n55: \n56: - [ ] **`WriteSession` implementation**: Agent must implement `WriteSession(AgentSession)` to restore sessions\n57: - [ ] **File-based agents** (Claude, Gemini, Cursor, Factory AI Droid, Copilot CLI): Write `NativeData` to `SessionRef` path\n58: - [ ] **Database-backed agents** (OpenCode): Write `NativeData` to file, then import into native storage (the native format should be what the agent's import command expects)\n59: - [ ] **Single format per agent**: Store only the agent's native format in `NativeData` - no separate fields for different representations of the same data\n60: \n61: ### Hook Events\n62: \n63: See Guide: [Step 4 - ParseHookEvent](agent-guide.md#step-4-implement-parsehookevent-lifecyclego), [Event Mapping Reference](agent-guide.md#event-mapping-reference)\n64: \n65: Map agent-native hooks to these `EventType` constants (see `agent/event.go`):\n66: \n67: - [ ] **TurnStart**: Fire when user submits a prompt (for pre-prompt state capture)\n68: - [ ] **TurnEnd**: Fire when agent finishes responding (for checkpoint creation)\n69: - [ ] **SessionStart**: Fire when a new session begins\n70: - [ ] **SessionEnd**: Fire when session is explicitly ended (optional but recommended)\n71: \n72: ### Rewind/Resume Support\n73: \n74: - [ ] **Rewind restores full state**: After rewind, agent can continue from that point with full context\n75: - [ ] **Resume command**: `FormatResumeCommand()` returns the CLI command to resume a session\n76: - [ ] **Session ID preservation**: Restored sessions maintain original session ID where possible\n77: \n78: ### Testing\n79: \n80: See Guide: [Testing Patterns](agent-guide.md#testing-patterns)\n81: \n82: - [ ] **New session**: Create session, multiple turns, verify full transcript at each checkpoint\n83: - [ ] **Resumed session**: Resume existing session, add turns, verify checkpoint includes historical messages\n84: - [ ] **Rewind**: Rewind to earlier checkpoint, verify agent can continue from that state\n85: - [ ] **Agent shutdown**: Verify graceful handling if agent exits during checkpoint\n86: - [ ] **Manual token validation for session-wide aggregate agents**: If an agent emits authoritative token totals only at session end (for example Copilot CLI `session.shutdown`), manually verify checkpoint-scoped metadata and full-session status separately. See [Copilot Token Validation](copilot-token-validation.md).\n\n(End of file - total 86 lines)\n</content>",
