            "output": "<path>/Users/aasheesh/Documents/webdev/os/cli/docs/FEATURE_PROPOSAL_searchable_prompts.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Feature Proposal: Searchable Prompts & Intent Review CLI\n2: \n3: ## Executive Summary\n4: \n5: **Goal:** Implement CLI commands that let users search their checkpoint history by *what they asked the agent*, not just what code changed.\n6: \n7: **Problem:** Developers can search code (git blame, grep) but cannot search *intent* - the prompts that led to decisions. \"Why did we use this library?\" → need to find the prompt, not the code.\n8: \n9: **Roadmap Alignment:** Entire explicitly listed \"searchable prompts\" and \"intent review\" as future goals (March 2026 roadmap).\n10: \n11: ---\n12: \n13: ## Part 1: Current Product State\n14: \n15: ### What's Already Built\n16: \n17: #### Checkpoint System\n18: - Captures: transcripts, prompts, files touched, token usage, timestamps\n19: - Storage: Git branch (`entire/checkpoints/v1`)\n20: - Metadata structure (from `checkpoint.go`):\n21:   ```go\n22:   type CheckpointSummary struct {\n23:       CheckpointID  string\n24:       FilesTouched []string\n25:       Sessions      []SessionInfo\n26:       // NO PROMPT FIELD at summary level\n27:   }\n28:   \n29:   type SessionContent struct {\n30:       Transcript   []byte\n31:       Prompts      []string  // Stored but not indexed\n32:       Metadata     CommittedMetadata\n33:   }\n34:   \n35:   type CommittedMetadata struct {\n36:       Kind        string   // \"session\" | \"agent_review\"\n37:       ReviewSkills []string\n38:       ReviewPrompt string\n39:   }\n40:   ```\n41: \n42: #### Existing Search (`entire search`)\n43: - Uses external search API (entire.io service)\n44: - Searches code/diffs, not prompts\n45: - Requires authentication\n46: - Based on hybrid semantic + keyword search\n47: \n48: #### Existing Review (`entire review`)\n49: - Runs configured review skills against branch\n50: - Multi-agent support (TUI with Bubble Tea)\n51: - Review sessions tagged in checkpoints\n52: - NOT \"intent-first\" - still diff-centric\n53: \n54: #### Skills System (New - May 2026)\n55: - Agents can search their own history via skills\n56: - `search` skill for agents\n57: - `explain` skill for agents\n58: - Cross-agent compatible\n59: - **For agents, not users**\n60: \n61: ---\n62: \n63: ## Part 2: Roadmap Status\n64: \n65: ### From March 25, 2026 Blog: \"The Entire CLI: How It Works & Where It's Headed\"\n66: \n67: | Feature | Status | Notes |\n68: |---------|--------|-------|\n69: | **Team Visibility** | Not shipped | \"Git tells you who committed. Entire shows how it was built.\" |\n70: | **Searchable Prompts** | **NOT SHIPPED** | \"surfacing the prompt that introduced a workaround\" |\n71: | **Audit Attribution** | Partial | Line-level attribution exists; full audit trail in progress |\n72: | **Intent Review** | **NOT SHIPPED** | \"moving beyond the diff to replace code reviews with intent reviews\" |\n73: \n74: ### From May 7, 2026 Blog: \"Bring Structure to Your Agent Workflows\"\n75: - `entire labs` command for experimental workflows\n76: - `entire recap` command for browsing recaps\n77: - `entire review` command (skills-based)\n78: - Skills system for agents to search history\n79: \n80: **Key Finding:** Skills are for *agents* to search. Users still cannot search prompts via CLI.\n81: \n82: ---\n83: \n84: ## Part 3: The Gap\n85: \n86: ### Problem Statement\n87: \n88: **User need:** \"I need to find when we decided to use Redis instead of Memcached\"\n89: \n90: **Current workflow:**\n91: 1. Grep for \"redis\" in code → finds usage, not *decision*\n92: 2. Git blame → shows who, not *why*\n93: 3. Check Slack/Notion/Google Docs → fragmented\n94: 4. Ask teammates → unreliable\n95: \n96: **With searchable prompts:**\n97: ```bash\n98: entire prompts search \"cache\"\n99: # → \"Why did we choose Redis over Memcached?\" - 2026-03-15\n100: # → \"Add Redis caching for session store\" - 2026-04-02\n101: ```\n102: \n103: ### User Stories\n104: \n105: 1. **Investigate regression:** \"This auth flow is complex. Find when we discussed it.\"\n106: 2. **Understand decisions:** \"Why did we pick this library? What was the context?\"\n107: 3. **Find similar work:** \"Has anyone worked on OAuth before?\"\n108: 4. **Onboarding:** \"Show me how this feature was built\"\n109: 5. **Audit:** \"What prompts led to this security fix?\"\n110: \n111: ---\n112: \n113: ## Part 4: Proposed Solution\n114: \n115: ### Option A: `entire prompts` Command (Recommended)\n116: \n117: **New command structure:**\n118: ```bash\n119: entire prompts list                    # List recent prompts\n120: entire prompts search <query>          # Search prompts\n121: entire prompts show <checkpoint-id>   # Show prompt for checkpoint\n122: entire prompts diff <checkpoint-id>   # Show prompt + diff together\n123: ```\n124: \n125: **Why Option A:**\n126: - Clear, discoverable namespace\n127: - Mirrors `entire checkpoint` structure\n128: - Extends existing architecture\n129: \n130: ### Option B: Extend `entire search` with `--prompts`\n131: \n132: ```bash\n133: entire search --prompts \"cache\"       # Search prompts only\n134: entire search --both \"cache\"         # Search both prompts and code\n135: ```\n136: \n137: **Why not Option B:**\n138: - Search already requires auth + API\n139: - Prompts are local (git branch), should work offline\n140: - Different use case: search vs explore\n141: \n142: ---\n143: \n144: ## Part 5: Technical Architecture\n145: \n146: ### Data Flow\n147: \n148: ```\n149: Checkpoint Created\n150:     ↓\n151: Prompts Extracted from Transcript\n152:     ↓\n153: Stored in Git Branch\n154:     ├── Prompt text (full)\n155:     ├── Embedding vector (future)\n156:     └── Metadata (checkpoint_id, session_id, timestamp)\n157:     ↓\n158: User Queries\n159:     ↓\n160: Local Index (SQLite) ← New component\n161:     ↓\n162: Results Displayed\n163: ```\n164: \n165: ### Components to Build\n166: \n167: ```\n168: cmd/entire/cli/prompts/\n169: ├── prompts.go           # Main command group\n170: ├── list.go             # entire prompts list\n171: ├── search.go           # entire prompts search  \n172: ├── show.go             # entire prompts show\n173: ├── diff.go             # entire prompts diff (prompt + files)\n174: ├── indexer.go          # Build/update local prompt index\n175: ├── store.go            # SQLite-based prompt storage\n176: ├── embed.go            # (Future) Embedding generation\n177: └── test/\n178:     ├── prompts_test.go\n179:     ├── search_test.go\n180:     └── indexer_test.go\n181: ```\n182: \n183: ### Data Model\n184: \n185: ```go\n186: // Local prompt store\n187: type PromptStore struct {\n188:     db *sql.DB\n189: }\n190: \n191: type Prompt struct {\n192:     ID            string    // UUID\n193:     CheckpointID  string    // From checkpoint\n194:     SessionID     string    // From session\n195:     Text          string    // Full prompt text\n196:     Timestamp     time.Time\n197:     Agent         string    // \"Claude Code\", etc.\n198:     Model         string    // \"claude-opus-4\"\n199:     FilesChanged  []string // Files in this checkpoint\n200:     Branch        string\n201:     Author        string    // Git author\n202: }\n203: \n204: type SearchResult struct {\n205:     Prompt   Prompt\n206:     Score    float64      // Similarity score\n207:     Matches  []string     // Matching terms\n208:     Context  string       // Surrounding context (files)\n209: }\n210: ```\n211: \n212: ### Index Strategy\n213: \n214: **Phase 1: Full-text search (immediate)**\n215: ```sql\n216: CREATE VIRTUAL TABLE prompts USING fts5(\n217:     text,\n218:     checkpoint_id UNINDEXED,\n219:     session_id UNINDEXED\n220: );\n221: ```\n222: \n223: **Phase 2: Semantic search (future)**\n224: - Generate embeddings from prompts\n225: - Store vectors alongside text\n226: - Use cosine similarity for ranking\n227: - Can use local model (llama.cpp) or API\n228: \n229: **Phase 3: Cross-repo search (future)**\n230: - Push index to checkpoint remote\n231: - Search across team's history\n232: - Privacy controls\n233: \n234: ---\n235: \n236: ## Part 6: Algorithms & Methods\n237: \n238: ### Search Algorithm Comparison\n239: \n240: | Algorithm | Pros | Cons | Recommendation |\n241: |-----------|------|------|----------------|\n242: | **BM25** | Fast, good for keyword | No semantic understanding | Phase 1 fallback |\n243: | **TF-IDF** | Simple, interpretable | Ignores word order | Not recommended |\n244: | **Dense Retrieval** | Semantic matching | Needs embeddings | Phase 2 |\n245: | **Hybrid (BM25 + Dense)** | Best of both | Complexity | Phase 2+ |\n246: \n247: ### Recommended Approach: TF-IDF + Trigram (Phase 1)\n248: \n249: ```go\n250: // Simple but effective for local prompts\n251: // Based on PostgreSQL's pg_trgm + ts_rank pattern\n252: \n253: type PromptSearcher struct {\n254:     db *sql.DB\n255: }\n256: \n257: func (s *PromptSearcher) Search(query string, limit int) ([]Prompt, error) {\n258:     // 1. Tokenize query\n259:     tokens := tokenize(query)\n260:     \n261:     // 2. Build weighted SQL query\n262:     // - Exact phrase matches: high weight\n263:     // - Individual word matches: medium weight\n264:     // - All tokens must match (AND semantics)\n265:     \n266:     sql := `\n267:         SELECT p.*, \n268:             ts_rank(to_tsvector('english', p.text), query) as rank\n269:         FROM prompts p, to_tsquery('english', ?) as query\n270:         WHERE to_tsvector('english', p.text) @@ query\n271:         ORDER BY rank DESC\n272:         LIMIT ?\n273:     `\n274:     \n275:     return s.db.Query(sql, tokens, limit)\n276: }\n277: ```\n278: \n279: ### Semantic Search (Phase 2)\n280: \n281: **Option 1: Local embeddings (Privacy-first)**\n282: ```bash\n283: # Embedding model (quantized, ~1GB)\n284: sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2\n285: ```\n286: \n287: **Option 2: API-based (Simpler)**\n288: ```bash\n289: # Use existing provider\n290: openai embeddings / anthropic embeddings\n291: ```\n292: \n293: **Hybrid Ranking Formula:**\n294: ```\n295: FinalScore = α × BM25Score + (1-α) × CosineSimilarity\n296: ```\n297: - α = 0.3 for prompts (semantic > keyword)\n298: \n299: ---\n300: \n301: ## Part 7: Edge Cases\n302: \n303: ### 1. Large Transcripts\n304: - **Problem:** Single session can have 100+ prompts\n305: - **Solution:** Index all prompts; show session grouping in results\n306: \n307: ### 2. Multi-turn Context\n308: - **Problem:** \"Continue\" or follow-up prompts lack full context\n309: - **Solution:** Include parent prompt reference; show conversation thread\n310: \n311: ### 3. Binary/File Prompts\n312: - **Problem:** Some prompts are just \"fix tests\" with no detail\n313: - **Solution:** Use checkpoint description as fallback; warn on weak prompts\n314: \n315: ### 4. Non-English Prompts\n316: - **Problem:** Tokenizers/embeddings may not handle mixed languages\n317: - **Solution:** UTF-8 support; language detection; separate indexes\n318: \n319: ### 5. Privacy/Sensitive Prompts\n320: - **Problem:** Prompts may contain secrets, PII\n321: - **Solution:** Re-use existing PII redaction; exclude from index option\n322: \n323: ### 6. Offline Mode\n324: - **Problem:** User disconnected from internet\n325: - **Solution:** Local SQLite index works offline; cross-repo needs connectivity\n326: \n327: ### 7. Fresh Index\n328: - **Problem:** No prompts indexed yet\n329: - **Solution:** Index built incrementally; initial build is background job\n330: \n331: ### 8. Merge Conflicts\n332: - **Problem:** Multiple checkpoints condensed\n333: - **Solution:** Index uses checkpoint_id, not commit order; dedup by ID\n334: \n335: ### 9. Session Resume\n336: - **Problem:** Resumed sessions have different checkpoint IDs\n337: - **Solution:** Link resumed sessions via PreviousSessionID\n338: \n339: ### 10. Deleted/Pruned Checkpoints\n340: - **Problem:** Checkpoint deleted,