            "output": "<path>/Users/aasheesh/Documents/webdev/os/cli/CONTRIBUTING.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Contributing to the Entire CLI\n2: \n3: Thank you for your interest in contributing to Entire! We welcome contributions from everyone.\n4: \n5: Please read our [Code of Conduct](CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) before participating.\n6: \n7: > **New to Entire?** See the [README](README.md) for setup and usage documentation.\n8: \n9: ---\n10: \n11: ## Before You Code: Discuss First\n12: \n13: The fastest way to get a contribution merged is to align with maintainers before writing code. Please **open an issue first** using our [issue templates](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues/new/choose) and wait for maintainer feedback before starting implementation.\n14: \n15: ### Contribution Workflow\n16: \n17: 1. **Open an issue** describing the problem or feature\n18: 2. **Wait for maintainer feedback** -- we may have relevant context or plans\n19: 3. **Get approval** before starting implementation\n20: 4. **Submit your PR** referencing the approved issue\n21: 5. **Address all feedback** including automated Copilot comments\n22: 6. **Maintainer review and merge**\n23: \n24: ---\n25: \n26: ## First-Time Contributors\n27: \n28: New to the project? Welcome! Here's how to get started:\n29: \n30: ### Good First Issues\n31: \n32: We recommend starting with:\n33: - **Documentation improvements** - Fix typos, clarify explanations, add examples\n34: - **Test contributions** - Add test cases, improve coverage\n35: - **Small bug fixes** - Issues labeled `good-first-issue`\n36: \n37: ---\n38: \n39: ## Submitting Issues\n40: \n41: All feature requests, bug reports, and general issues should be submitted through [GitHub Issues](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues). Please search for existing issues before opening a new one.\n42: \n43: For security-related issues, see the Security section below.\n44: \n45: ---\n46: \n47: ## Security\n48: \n49: If you discover a security vulnerability, **do not report it through GitHub Issues**. Instead, please follow the instructions in our [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md) file for responsible disclosure. All security reports are kept confidential as described in SECURITY.md.\n50: \n51: ---\n52: \n53: ## Contributions & Communication\n54: \n55: Contributions and communications are expected to occur through:\n56: \n57: - [GitHub Issues](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues) - Bug reports and feature requests\n58: - [Discord](https://discord.gg/jZJs3Tue4S) - Questions, general conversation, and real-time support\n59: \n60: Please represent the project and community respectfully in all public and private interactions.\n61: \n62: \n63: ## How to Contribute\n64: \n65: \n66: There are many ways to contribute:\n67: \n68: - **Feature requests** - Open a [GitHub Issue](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues) to discuss your idea\n69: - **Bug reports** - Report issues via [GitHub Issues](https://github.com/entireio/cli/issues) (see [Reporting Bugs](#reporting-bugs))\n70: - **Code contributions** - Fix bugs, add features, improve tests\n71: - **Documentation** - Improve guides, fix typos, add examples\n72: - **Community** - Help others, answer questions, share knowledge\n73: \n74: \n75: ## Reporting Bugs\n76: \n77: Good bug reports help us fix issues quickly. When reporting a bug, please include:\n78: \n79: ### Required Information\n80: \n81: 1. **Entire CLI version** - run `entire version`\n82: 2. **Operating system**\n83: 3. **Go version** - run `go version`\n84: \n85: ### What to Include\n86: \n87: Please answer these questions in your bug report:\n88: \n89: 1. **What did you do?** - Include the exact commands you ran\n90: 2. **What did you expect to happen?**\n91: 3. **What actually happened?** - Include the full error message or unexpected output\n92: 4. **Can you reproduce it?** - Does it happen every time or intermittently?\n93: 5. **Any additional context?** - Logs, screenshots, or related issues\n94: \n95: ---\n96: \n97: ## Local Setup\n98: \n99: ### Prerequisites\n100: \n101: - **Go 1.26.x** - Check with `go version`\n102: - **mise** - Task runner and version manager. Install with `curl https://mise.run | sh`\n103: \n104: ### Clone and Install\n105: \n106: ```bash\n107: # Clone the repository\n108: git clone https://github.com/entireio/cli.git\n109: cd cli\n110: \n111: # Trust the mise configuration (required on first setup)\n112: mise trust\n113: \n114: # Install dependencies (mise will install the correct Go version)\n115: mise install\n116: \n117: # Download Go modules\n118: go mod download\n119: \n120: # Build the CLI\n121: mise run build\n122: \n123: # Verify setup by running tests\n124: mise run test\n125: ```\n126: \n127: > See [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md) for detailed architecture and development reference.\n128: \n129: ---\n130: \n131: ## Making Changes\n132: \n133: 1. **Create a branch** for your changes:\n134:    ```bash\n135:    git checkout -b feature/your-feature-name\n136:    ```\n137: \n138: 2. **Make your changes** - follow the [Code Style](#code-style) guidelines\n139: \n140: 3. **Test your changes** - see [Testing](#testing)\n141: \n142: 4. **Commit** with clear, descriptive messages:\n143:    ```bash\n144:    git commit -m \"Add feature: description of what you added\"\n145:    ```\n146: \n147: ---\n148: \n149: ## Code Style\n150: \n151: Follow standard Go idioms and conventions. For detailed guidance, see the **Go Code Style** section in [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md).\n152: \n153: ### Key Points\n154: \n155: - **Error handling**: Handle all errors explicitly - don't leave them unchecked\n156: - **Formatting**: Code must pass `gofmt` (run `mise run fmt`)\n157: - **Linting**: Code must pass `golangci-lint` (run `mise run lint`)\n158: - **Naming**: Use meaningful, descriptive names following Go conventions\n159: \n160: ---\n161: \n162: ## Testing\n163: \n164: > See [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md) for complete testing documentation.\n165: \n166: ```bash\n167: # Unit tests - always run before committing\n168: mise run test\n169: \n170: # Integration tests\n171: mise run test:integration\n172: \n173: # Full CI suite\n174: mise run test:ci\n175: ```\n176: \n177: Integration tests use the `//go:build integration` build tag and are located in `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/`.\n178: \n179: ---\n180: \n181: ## Creating an Agent\n182: \n183: \n184: Entire supports two ways to create agents:\n185: \n186: ### 1. Claude Code Agent Personas (Markdown)\n187: \n188: These are markdown files that define specialized behaviors for Claude Code (e.g., developer, reviewer, etc.).\n189: \n190: - **Location:** `.claude/agents/`\n191: - **Structure:**\n192:    ```markdown\n193:    ---\n194:    name: my-agent\n195:    description: What this agent does\n196:    model: opus\n197:    color: blue\n198:    ---\n199: \n200:    # Agent Name\n201:    You are a **[Role]** with expertise in [domain].\n202: \n203:    ## Core Principles\n204:    - Principle 1\n205:    - Principle 2\n206: \n207:    ## Process\n208:    1. Step 1\n209:    2. Step 2\n210: \n211:    ## Output Format\n212:    How to structure responses...\n213:    ```\n214: - **To invoke:** Create a matching command in `.claude/commands/` that spawns the agent via the Task tool.\n215: - **Examples:**\n216:    - `.claude/agents/dev.md` - TDD Developer\n217:    - `.claude/agents/reviewer.md` - Code Reviewer\n218: \n219: ### 2. Coding Agent Integrations (Go)\n220: \n221: These are Go implementations that integrate Entire with different AI coding tools (Claude Code, Gemini CLI, OpenCode, Cursor, Factory AI Droid, Copilot CLI, etc.) using the Agent abstraction layer.\n222: \n223: - **Location:** `cmd/entire/cli/agent/`\n224: - **Steps:**\n225:    1. Implement the `Agent` interface in `agent/agent.go`\n226:    2. Register your agent in the agent registry\n227:    3. Add setup and hook configuration as needed\n228:    4. Ensure session and checkpoint tracking is handled per the abstraction\n229: - **Reference:** See [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md) for architecture and code examples.\n230: \n231: ---\n232: \n233: **Which should I use?**\n234: \n235: - Use a persona markdown agent if you want to create a new role or workflow for Claude Code.\n236: - Use a coding agent integration if you want to add support for a new AI coding tool or extend agent capabilities in the CLI.\n237: \n238: ---\n239: \n240: ## Submitting a Pull Request\n241: \n242: ### Before You Submit\n243: \n244: - **Related issue exists and is approved** -- Your PR references an issue where a maintainer has acknowledged the approach. (Exceptions: documentation fixes, typo corrections, and `good-first-issue` items.)\n245: - **Linting passes** -- Run `mise run lint` (includes golangci-lint, gofmt, gomod, shellcheck)\n246: - **Tests pass** -- Run `mise run test` to verify your changes\n247: - **Tests included** -- New Go code and functionality should have accompanying tests\n248: - **Entire checkpoint trailers included** -- See [Using Entire While Contributing](#using-entire-while-contributing) below\n249: \n250: PRs that skip these steps are likely to be closed without merge.\n251: \n252: ### Submitting\n253: \n254: 1. **Push** your branch to your fork\n255: 2. **Open a PR** against the `main` branch\n256: 3. **Describe your changes** -- Link the related issue, summarize what changed and what testing you did\n257: 4. **Address Copilot feedback** -- See [Responding to Automated Review](#responding-to-automated-review)\n258: 5. **Wait for maintainer review**\n259: \n260: ---\n261: \n262: ## Responding to Automated Review\n263: \n264: Co-pilot agent reviews every PR and provides feedback on code quality, potential bugs, and project conventions.\n265: \n266: **Read and respond to every Copilot comment.** PRs with unaddressed Copilot feedback will not move to maintainer review.\n267: \n268: - **Fixed** -- Push a commit addressing the issue.\n269: - **Disagree** -- Reply explaining your reasoning. The Copilot isn't always right.\n270: - **Question** -- Ask for clarification. We're happy to help.\n271: \n272: Addressing Copilot feedback upfront is the fastest path to maintainer review.\n273: \n274: ---\n275: \n276: ## Using Entire While Contributing\n277: \n278: We use Entire on Entire. When contributing, install the Entire CLI and let it capture your coding sessions -- this gives us valuable dogfooding data and helps improve the tool.\n279: \n280: ### Setup\n281: \n282: Install the latest version of the Entire CLI (see [installation docs](https://docs.entire.io/cli/installation)) and verify with `entire version`. Entire is already configured in this repository, so there's no need to run `entire enable`.\n283: \n284: ### Checkpoint Trailers\n285: \n286: All commits should include `Entire-Checkpoint` trailers from your sessions. These are added automatically by the `prepare-commit-msg` hook when Entire is enabled. The trailers link your commits to session metadata on the `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch.\n287: \n288: ### Sessions Branch\n289: \n290: When you push your PR branch, Entire can automatically push the `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch alongside it (if `push_sessions` is enabled in your settings). Include this in your PR so maintainers can review the session context behind your changes.\n291: \n292: ---\n293: \n294: ## Troubleshooting\n295: \n296: ### Common Setup Issues\n297: \n298: **`go mod download` fails with timeout**\n299: ```bash\n300: # Try using direct mode\n301: GOPROXY=direct go mod download\n302: ```\n303: \n304: **`mise install` fails**\n305: ```bash\n306: # Ensure mise is properly installed\n307: curl https://mise.run | sh\n308: \n309: # Reload your shell\n310: source ~/.zshrc  # or ~/.bashrc\n311: ```\n312: \n313: **Binary not updating after rebuild**\n314: ```bash\n315: # Check which binary is being used\n316: which entire\n317: type -a entire\n318: \n319: # You may have multiple installations - update the correct path\n320: ```\n321: \n322: ---\n323: \n324: ## Community\n325: \n326: Join the Entire community:\n327: \n328: - **Discord** - [Join our server][discord] for discussions and support\n329: \n330: [discord]: https://discord.gg/jZJs3Tue4S\n331: \n332: ---\n333: \n334: ## Additional Resources\n335: \n336: - [README](README.md) - Setup and usage documentation\n337: - [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md) - Architecture and development reference (Claude Code)\n338: - [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) - Architecture and development reference (Gemini CLI, OpenCode, Cursor, Factory AI Droid, Copilot CLI)\n339: - [Code of Conduct](CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) - Community guidelines\n340: - [Security Policy](SECURITY.md) - Reporting security vulnerabilities\n341: \n342: ---\n343: \n344: Thank you for contributing!\n\n(End of file - total 344 lines)\n</content>",
