              "content": "# Feature: Searchable Prompts CLI (`entire prompts`)\n\n**Source of truth for implementation.** All decisions, design choices, and acceptance criteria are documented here. Update this doc when decisions change.\n\n- **GitHub Issue:** #1187\n- **Roadmap:** https://entire.io/blog/the-entire-cli-how-it-works-and-where-its-headed\n- **Feature Proposal:** `docs/FEATURE_PROPOSAL_searchable_prompts.md`\n\n---\n\n## 1. Problem\n\nDevelopers can search **what changed** but cannot search **why it changed** — the prompts and reasoning behind decisions.\n\n> \"We're making that answer searchable. Users will be able to surface the prompt that introduced a workaround or revisit the reasoning behind a library choice months later. The 'why' will be part of your history.\" — Entire Roadmap\n\n---\n\n## 2. Scope\n\n### In Scope (Phase 1)\n- `entire prompts search <query>` — keyword search over prompt history\n- `entire prompts list` — list recent prompts\n- `entire prompts show <checkpoint-id>` — show full prompt from git\n- `entire prompts index` — rebuild / status / verify\n\n### Out of Scope\n- Cross-repo search\n- Semantic/embedding search\n- Web platform integration\n- Non-English stop words\n\n---\n\n## 3. Architecture\n\n### Index Design\n\n**File:** `.entire/prompts/index.ndjson` (gitignored, local to this checkout)\n\n**Why `.ndjson` over JSON:**\n- gzip is a stream format — cannot append to it. Every update would require full read → decompress → modify → compress → rewrite.\n- `.ndjson` is appendable — new entries are single-line appends, no full rewrites.\n\n**Schema:**\n```go\n// Header — first line of the file\ntype IndexHeader struct {\n    Version   int       `json:\"version\"`    // format version (1)\n    CreatedAt time.Time `json:\"created_at\"`\n    RepoRoot  string    `json:\"repo_root\"`  // sanity check\n}\n\n// Each subsequent line is one entry\ntype PromptEntry struct {\n    CheckpointID      string    `json:\"checkpoint_id\"`    // \"a3b2c4d5e6f7\"\n    SessionIndex      int       `json:\"session_index\"`    // 0, 1, 2 (multi-session)\n    TurnIndex         int       `json:\"turn_index\"`       // 0, 1, 2 (multi-turn)\n    Kind              string    `json:\"kind\"`             // \"session\" | \"agent_review\"\n    PromptText        string    `json:\"prompt_text\"`      // truncated to 2000 chars\n    PromptTruncated   bool      `json:\"prompt_truncated\"`\n    CommitHash        string    `json:\"commit_hash\"`\n    CommitMessage     string    `json:\"commit_message\"`   // first line only\n    Branch            string    `json:\"branch\"`\n    Agent             string    `json:\"agent\"`            // \"Claude Code\"\n    Model             string    `json:\"model\"`\n    TokenCount        int       `json:\"token_count\"`\n    ParentCheckpointID string  `json:\"parent_checkpoint_id,omitempty\"`\n    SubagentDepth     int       `json:\"subagent_depth\"`\n    FilesTouched      []string  `json:\"files_touched\"`\n    CreatedAt         time.Time `json:\"created_at\"`\n}\n```\n\n**Index version constant:**\n```go\nconst CurrentIndexVersion = 1\n```\n\n**Version migration:** On `version < CurrentIndexVersion` or parse error, delete index and rebuild.\n\n### Package Structure\n\n```\ncmd/entire/cli/prompts/\n├── prompts.go        # Command group registration\n├── search.go         # entire prompts search\n├── list.go           # entire prompts list\n├── show.go           # entire prompts show\n├── index_cmd.go      # entire prompts index\n└── index/\n    ├── schema.go     # IndexHeader, PromptEntry types\n    ├── store.go      # read/append/rebuild, file locking\n    ├── builder.go    # walk checkpoint tree, multi-turn parsing\n    └── rank.go       # tokenizer, stemmer, scorer\n```\n\n### Multi-Worktree Support\n\nIndex lives at `<worktree-git-dir>/../.entire/prompts/index.ndjson` so concurrent worktrees have independent indexes.\n\n### Decoupled Checkpoint Repo\n\nWhen `checkpoint.remote` is configured, `IndexPath()` reads that config to resolve the checkpoint repo location.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Search Algorithm\n\n### Tokenizer\n\n```go\nfunc Tokenize(text string) []string {\n    // 1. Unicode normalization (NFC)\n    normalized := norm.NFC.String(strings.ToLower(text))\n    // 2. Split on non-word characters (regex)\n    tokens := wordBoundary.Split(normalized, -1)\n    // 3. Stem each token (Porter stemmer)\n    stemmed := make([]string, 0, len(tokens))\n    for _, t := range tokens {\n        if len(t) < 2 { continue }       // skip single chars\n        if stopWords[t] { continue }       // skip stop words\n        stemmed = append(stemmed, stem.Stem(t))\n    }\n    return stemmed\n}\n```\n\n**Stemmer:** `github.com/kljensen/snowball` — pure Go, zero CGO, MIT license.\n\n**Why stemming matters:**\n- `\"caching\"` → stems to `\"cach\"` → matches `\"cache\"`, `\"cached\"`, `\"caches\"`\n- `\"authenticated\"` → stems to `\"authent\"` → matches `\"auth\"`, `\"authentication\"`\n- Without stemming, ~30–40% of valid matches return zero results\n\n### Scorer\n\nWeighted keyword scoring with term-density normalization:\n\n```\nTermDensity = matched_token_count / total_prompt_token_count\n\nScore = (exact_phrase_match * 10)\n      + (all_query_tokens_found * 5)\n      + (any_query_token_found * 1)\n      + (TermDensity * 2)\n```\n\n**Within same score tier:** newer `CreatedAt` first.\n\n**Minimum query length:** 2 characters after tokenization. Early return with error: `\"query too short — enter at least one word\"`.\n\n**Special character handling:** Strip regex metacharacters before tokenization. Not interpreted as patterns.\n\n**Quoted phrase handling:** `\"redis cache\"` parsed as phrase, matched as adjacent sequence in stemmed token stream.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Commands\n\n### `entire prompts search`\n\n```\nentire prompts search <query>\nentire prompts search \"redis cache\"\nentire prompts search --limit 50\nentire prompts search --json\nentire prompts search --agent claude\nentire prompts search --branch feat/auth\nentire prompts search --after 2026-03-01\nentire prompts search --files cache/redis.go\nentire prompts search --kind agent_review\n```\n\n**Output:**\n```\nSearch results for \"redis cache\"  (23 found, showing 20)\n\n  a3b2c4d5e6f7  2026-03-15  Claude Code  main\n  \"Why did we choose Redis over Memcached for the caching layer?\"\n\n  7f8e9d1a2b3c  2026-04-02  Gemini CLI   feat/cache\n  \"Add Redis caching for session store to improve latency\"\n```\n\n### `entire prompts list`\n\n```\nentire prompts list               # last 20, newest first\nentire prompts list --limit 50\nentire prompts list --checkpoint abc123\nentire prompts list --cursor <token>   # cursor-based pagination\n```\n\n### `entire prompts show`\n\n```\nentire prompts show a3b2c4d5e6f7\nentire prompts show abc123              # prefix accepted\n```\n\n**Ambiguous prefix:** If short prefix matches multiple, list matches and ask to disambiguate.\n\n### `entire prompts index`\n\n```\nentire prompts index --rebuild   # full rebuild with progress bar\nentire prompts index --status    # checkpoint count, prompt count, orphans\nentire prompts index --verify    # check for orphaned entries\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. Data Flow\n\n### Index Update (at PostCommit hook)\n\n```\nUser commits → PostCommit hook fires\n      ↓\nstrategy.Condense() → WriteCommitted() writes checkpoint to git\n      ↓\nprompts.IndexBuilder.AppendFromCheckpoint(cpID, sessionIndex, sessionData)\n      ↓\nAcquire file lock (.entire/prompts/index.lock)\nAppend PromptEntry line to index.ndjson\nRelease lock\n```\n\n### Query (at search command)\n\n```\nentire prompts search \"redis cache\"\n      ↓\nLoadIndex() — read index.ndjson line by line\n  If missing → rebuild → reload\n  If version mismatch or parse error → rebuild → reload\n      ↓\nParseQuery() → handle quotes, strip special chars\nTokenizeQuery() → stem, remove stop words\n      ↓\nScore each PromptEntry (in-memory, no I/O after load)\nApply filters (--agent, --branch, --after, --files, --kind)\nSort by score desc, then CreatedAt desc\nSlice to --limit\n      ↓\nFormatResults() → TTY or JSON\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Edge Cases\n\n| # | Case | Handling |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Missing index | Auto-rebuild with progress bar, warn results may lag |\n| 2 | Corrupt index (parse error) | Delete, rebuild, log notice |\n| 3 | Index version mismatch | Delete, rebuild automatically |\n| 4 | Large prompts (>2000 chars) | Truncate in index, set `PromptTruncated=true` |\n| 5 | Match past truncation point | Result shown with note |\n| 6 | Multi-turn conversations | Each turn indexed separately with `TurnIndex` |\n| 7 | Agent review prompts | Indexed with `Kind=\"agent_review\"`, filterable with `--kind` |\n| 8 | Subagent checkpoints | `ParentCheckpointID` and `SubagentDepth` set |\n| 9 | Empty prompts | Skipped, count logged in `--status` |\n| 10 | Non-ASCII / Unicode | NFC normalization, `\"café\"` matches `\"cafe\"` |\n| 11 | Special chars in query | Stripped, not interpreted as regex |\n| 12 | Query too short | Early return with error |\n| 13 | Checkpoint deleted from git | `--verify` detects orphans, search skips silently |\n| 14 | Concurrent writes | File lock with retry backoff; NFS fallback to PID-lock |\n| 15 | Prefix ambiguity | List matches, prompt disambiguation |\n| 16 | `--json` in non-TTY | PII warning to stderr |\n\n---\n\n## 8. Concurrency\n\n### File Lock Pattern\n\n```go\nfunc (s *IndexStore) AppendEntry(entry PromptEntry) error {\n    lock, err := lockfile.New(s.LockPath()) // .entire/prompts/index.lock\n    if err != nil {\n        return err\n    }\n    if err := lock.TryLock(); err != nil {\n        return s.retryAppend(entry, 3) // max 3 attempts, 50ms backoff\n    }\n    defer lock.Unlock()\n    return s.appendLine(entry)\n}\n```\n\n### NFS Fallback\n\nDetect via `statfs`. If NFS, use `.lock` file with PID-based ownership check (same pattern as git).\n\n---\n\n## 9. Benchmarks\n\n| Operation | Target |\n|---|---|\n| Index load — 1K checkpoints | < 100ms |\n| Index load — 10K checkpoints | < 500ms |\n| Search — 1K checkpoints | < 20ms |\n| Search — 10K checkpoints | < 100ms |\n| Index append (new checkpoint) | < 50ms |\n| Full rebuild — 1K checkpoints | < 10s |\n\n---\n\n## 10. Testing Plan\n\n- **Unit tests:** scorer, tokenizer, tokenize/score edge cases\n- **Benchmark tests (`testing.B`):** `BenchmarkSearch1K`, `BenchmarkSearch10K`, `BenchmarkIndexLoad`\n- **Golden file tests:** CLI output formatting\n- **Integration tests:** temporary git repo with real checkpoint data\n- **Concurrent write test:** two goroutines writing simultaneously\n- **Edge case tests:** empty prompts, long prompts, multi-turn, unicode, special chars, corrupt index\n\n---\n\n## 11. Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `entire prompts search` < 100ms for 1K, < 500ms for 10K\n- [ ] Stemming active — \"caching\" matches \"cache\"\n- [ ] Multi-turn indexed per-turn with `TurnIndex`\n- [ ] `--json` in non-TTY emits PII warning to stderr\n- [ ] Concurrent writes do not corrupt index\n- [ ] Cold start auto-rebuild with progress bar\n- [ ] No new CGO dependencies\n- [ ] All benchmark targets met\n\n---\n\n## 12. New Dependencies\n\n- `github.com/kljensen/snowball` — pure Go Porter stemmer, MIT license, zero CGO\n\n---\n\n## 13. Integration Points\n\n1. **PostCommit hook** (`strategy/manual_commit_hooks.go`): After `writeCommitted` succeeds, call `prompts.IndexBuilder.AppendFromCheckpoint()`\n2. **`entire prompts index --rebuild`**: Walk `entire/checkpoints/v1` tree, read each session's `prompt.txt`, write fresh `index.ndjson`\n3. **`entire prompts show`**: Reads from git tree (not index) — uses `checkpoint/committed.go` methods\n\n---\n\n## 14. Implementation Checklist\n\n- [ ] `cmd/entire/cli/prompts/index/schema.go` — types\n- [ ] `cmd/entire/cli/prompts/index/store.go` — read/append/lock\n- [ ] `cmd/entire/cli/prompts/index/rank.go` — tokenizer/stemmer/scorer\n- [ ] `cmd/entire/cli/prompts/index/builder.go` — walk checkpoint tree\n- [ ] `cmd/entire/cli/prompts/prompts.go` — command group\n- [ ] `cmd/entire/cli/prompts/search.go` — search command\n- [ ] `cmd/entire/cli/prompts/list.go` — list command\n- [ ] `cmd/entire/cli/prompts/show.go` — show command\n- [ ] `cmd/entire/cli/prompts/index_cmd.go` — index command (rebuild/status/verify)\n- [ ] PostCommit hook integration\n- [ ] Unit tests + benchmarks\n- [ ] `mise run check` passes",
