            "output": "<path>/Users/aasheesh/Documents/webdev/os/cli/docs/FEATURE_prompts_search.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Feature: Searchable Prompts CLI (`entire prompts`)\n2: \n3: **Source of truth for implementation.** All decisions, design choices, and acceptance criteria are documented here. Update this doc when decisions change.\n4: \n5: - **GitHub Issue:** #1187\n6: - **Roadmap:** https://entire.io/blog/the-entire-cli-how-it-works-and-where-its-headed\n7: - **Feature Proposal:** `docs/FEATURE_PROPOSAL_searchable_prompts.md`\n8: \n9: ---\n10: \n11: ## 1. Problem\n12: \n13: Developers can search **what changed** but cannot search **why it changed** — the prompts and reasoning behind decisions.\n14: \n15: > \"We're making that answer searchable. Users will be able to surface the prompt that introduced a workaround or revisit the reasoning behind a library choice months later. The 'why' will be part of your history.\" — Entire Roadmap\n16: \n17: ---\n18: \n19: ## 2. Scope\n20: \n21: ### In Scope (Phase 1)\n22: - `entire prompts search <query>` — keyword search over prompt history\n23: - `entire prompts list` — list recent prompts\n24: - `entire prompts show <checkpoint-id>` — show full prompt from git\n25: - `entire prompts index` — rebuild / status / verify\n26: \n27: ### Out of Scope\n28: - Cross-repo search\n29: - Semantic/embedding search\n30: - Web platform integration\n31: - Non-English stop words\n32: \n33: ---\n34: \n35: ## 3. Architecture\n36: \n37: ### Index Design\n38: \n39: **File:** `.entire/prompts/index.ndjson` (gitignored, local to this checkout)\n40: \n41: **Why `.ndjson` over JSON:**\n42: - gzip is a stream format — cannot append to it. Every update would require full read → decompress → modify → compress → rewrite.\n43: - `.ndjson` is appendable — new entries are single-line appends, no full rewrites.\n44: \n45: **Schema:**\n46: ```go\n47: // Header — first line of the file\n48: type IndexHeader struct {\n49:     Version   int       `json:\"version\"`    // format version (1)\n50:     CreatedAt time.Time `json:\"created_at\"`\n51:     RepoRoot  string    `json:\"repo_root\"`  // sanity check\n52: }\n53: \n54: // Each subsequent line is one entry\n55: type PromptEntry struct {\n56:     CheckpointID      string    `json:\"checkpoint_id\"`    // \"a3b2c4d5e6f7\"\n57:     SessionIndex      int       `json:\"session_index\"`    // 0, 1, 2 (multi-session)\n58:     TurnIndex         int       `json:\"turn_index\"`       // 0, 1, 2 (multi-turn)\n59:     Kind              string    `json:\"kind\"`             // \"session\" | \"agent_review\"\n60:     PromptText        string    `json:\"prompt_text\"`      // truncated to 2000 chars\n61:     PromptTruncated   bool      `json:\"prompt_truncated\"`\n62:     CommitHash        string    `json:\"commit_hash\"`\n63:     CommitMessage     string    `json:\"commit_message\"`   // first line only\n64:     Branch            string    `json:\"branch\"`\n65:     Agent             string    `json:\"agent\"`            // \"Claude Code\"\n66:     Model             string    `json:\"model\"`\n67:     TokenCount        int       `json:\"token_count\"`\n68:     ParentCheckpointID string  `json:\"parent_checkpoint_id,omitempty\"`\n69:     SubagentDepth     int       `json:\"subagent_depth\"`\n70:     FilesTouched      []string  `json:\"files_touched\"`\n71:     CreatedAt         time.Time `json:\"created_at\"`\n72: }\n73: ```\n74: \n75: **Index version constant:**\n76: ```go\n77: const CurrentIndexVersion = 1\n78: ```\n79: \n80: **Version migration:** On `version < CurrentIndexVersion` or parse error, delete index and rebuild.\n81: \n82: ### Package Structure\n83: \n84: ```\n85: cmd/entire/cli/prompts/\n86: ├── prompts.go        # Command group registration\n87: ├── search.go         # entire prompts search\n88: ├── list.go           # entire prompts list\n89: ├── show.go           # entire prompts show\n90: ├── index_cmd.go      # entire prompts index\n91: └── index/\n92:     ├── schema.go     # IndexHeader, PromptEntry types\n93:     ├── store.go      # read/append/rebuild, file locking\n94:     ├── builder.go    # walk checkpoint tree, multi-turn parsing\n95:     └── rank.go       # tokenizer, stemmer, scorer\n96: ```\n97: \n98: ### Multi-Worktree Support\n99: \n100: Index lives at `<worktree-git-dir>/../.entire/prompts/index.ndjson` so concurrent worktrees have independent indexes.\n101: \n102: ### Decoupled Checkpoint Repo\n103: \n104: When `checkpoint.remote` is configured, `IndexPath()` reads that config to resolve the checkpoint repo location.\n105: \n106: ---\n107: \n108: ## 4. Search Algorithm\n109: \n110: ### Tokenizer\n111: \n112: ```go\n113: func Tokenize(text string) []string {\n114:     // 1. Unicode normalization (NFC)\n115:     normalized := norm.NFC.String(strings.ToLower(text))\n116:     // 2. Split on non-word characters (regex)\n117:     tokens := wordBoundary.Split(normalized, -1)\n118:     // 3. Stem each token (Porter stemmer)\n119:     stemmed := make([]string, 0, len(tokens))\n120:     for _, t := range tokens {\n121:         if len(t) < 2 { continue }       // skip single chars\n122:         if stopWords[t] { continue }       // skip stop words\n123:         stemmed = append(stemmed, stem.Stem(t))\n124:     }\n125:     return stemmed\n126: }\n127: ```\n128: \n129: **Stemmer:** `github.com/kljensen/snowball` — pure Go, zero CGO, MIT license.\n130: \n131: **Why stemming matters:**\n132: - `\"caching\"` → stems to `\"cach\"` → matches `\"cache\"`, `\"cached\"`, `\"caches\"`\n133: - `\"authenticated\"` → stems to `\"authent\"` → matches `\"auth\"`, `\"authentication\"`\n134: - Without stemming, ~30–40% of valid matches return zero results\n135: \n136: ### Scorer\n137: \n138: Weighted keyword scoring with term-density normalization:\n139: \n140: ```\n141: TermDensity = matched_token_count / total_prompt_token_count\n142: \n143: Score = (exact_phrase_match * 10)\n144:       + (all_query_tokens_found * 5)\n145:       + (any_query_token_found * 1)\n146:       + (TermDensity * 2)\n147: ```\n148: \n149: **Within same score tier:** newer `CreatedAt` first.\n150: \n151: **Minimum query length:** 2 characters after tokenization. Early return with error: `\"query too short — enter at least one word\"`.\n152: \n153: **Special character handling:** Strip regex metacharacters before tokenization. Not interpreted as patterns.\n154: \n155: **Quoted phrase handling:** `\"redis cache\"` parsed as phrase, matched as adjacent sequence in stemmed token stream.\n156: \n157: ---\n158: \n159: ## 5. Commands\n160: \n161: ### `entire prompts search`\n162: \n163: ```\n164: entire prompts search <query>\n165: entire prompts search \"redis cache\"\n166: entire prompts search --limit 50\n167: entire prompts search --json\n168: entire prompts search --agent claude\n169: entire prompts search --branch feat/auth\n170: entire prompts search --after 2026-03-01\n171: entire prompts search --files cache/redis.go\n172: entire prompts search --kind agent_review\n173: ```\n174: \n175: **Output:**\n176: ```\n177: Search results for \"redis cache\"  (23 found, showing 20)\n178: \n179:   a3b2c4d5e6f7  2026-03-15  Claude Code  main\n180:   \"Why did we choose Redis over Memcached for the caching layer?\"\n181: \n182:   7f8e9d1a2b3c  2026-04-02  Gemini CLI   feat/cache\n183:   \"Add Redis caching for session store to improve latency\"\n184: ```\n185: \n186: ### `entire prompts list`\n187: \n188: ```\n189: entire prompts list               # last 20, newest first\n190: entire prompts list --limit 50\n191: entire prompts list --checkpoint abc123\n192: entire prompts list --cursor <token>   # cursor-based pagination\n193: ```\n194: \n195: ### `entire prompts show`\n196: \n197: ```\n198: entire prompts show a3b2c4d5e6f7\n199: entire prompts show abc123              # prefix accepted\n200: ```\n201: \n202: **Ambiguous prefix:** If short prefix matches multiple, list matches and ask to disambiguate.\n203: \n204: ### `entire prompts index`\n205: \n206: ```\n207: entire prompts index --rebuild   # full rebuild with progress bar\n208: entire prompts index --status    # checkpoint count, prompt count, orphans\n209: entire prompts index --verify    # check for orphaned entries\n210: ```\n211: \n212: ---\n213: \n214: ## 6. Data Flow\n215: \n216: ### Index Update (at PostCommit hook)\n217: \n218: ```\n219: User commits → PostCommit hook fires\n220:       ↓\n221: strategy.Condense() → WriteCommitted() writes checkpoint to git\n222:       ↓\n223: prompts.IndexBuilder.AppendFromCheckpoint(cpID, sessionIndex, sessionData)\n224:       ↓\n225: Acquire file lock (.entire/prompts/index.lock)\n226: Append PromptEntry line to index.ndjson\n227: Release lock\n228: ```\n229: \n230: ### Query (at search command)\n231: \n232: ```\n233: entire prompts search \"redis cache\"\n234:       ↓\n235: LoadIndex() — read index.ndjson line by line\n236:   If missing → rebuild → reload\n237:   If version mismatch or parse error → rebuild → reload\n238:       ↓\n239: ParseQuery() → handle quotes, strip special chars\n240: TokenizeQuery() → stem, remove stop words\n241:       ↓\n242: Score each PromptEntry (in-memory, no I/O after load)\n243: Apply filters (--agent, --branch, --after, --files, --kind)\n244: Sort by score desc, then CreatedAt desc\n245: Slice to --limit\n246:       ↓\n247: FormatResults() → TTY or JSON\n248: ```\n249: \n250: ---\n251: \n252: ## 7. Edge Cases\n253: \n254: | # | Case | Handling |\n255: |---|---|---|\n256: | 1 | Missing index | Auto-rebuild with progress bar, warn results may lag |\n257: | 2 | Corrupt index (parse error) | Delete, rebuild, log notice |\n258: | 3 | Index version mismatch | Delete, rebuild automatically |\n259: | 4 | Large prompts (>2000 chars) | Truncate in index, set `PromptTruncated=true` |\n260: | 5 | Match past truncation point | Result shown with note |\n261: | 6 | Multi-turn conversations | Each turn indexed separately with `TurnIndex` |\n262: | 7 | Agent review prompts | Indexed with `Kind=\"agent_review\"`, filterable with `--kind` |\n263: | 8 | Subagent checkpoints | `ParentCheckpointID` and `SubagentDepth` set |\n264: | 9 | Empty prompts | Skipped, count logged in `--status` |\n265: | 10 | Non-ASCII / Unicode | NFC normalization, `\"café\"` matches `\"cafe\"` |\n266: | 11 | Special chars in query | Stripped, not interpreted as regex |\n267: | 12 | Query too short | Early return with error |\n268: | 13 | Checkpoint deleted from git | `--verify` detects orphans, search skips silently |\n269: | 14 | Concurrent writes | File lock with retry backoff; NFS fallback to PID-lock |\n270: | 15 | Prefix ambiguity | List matches, prompt disambiguation |\n271: | 16 | `--json` in non-TTY | PII warning to stderr |\n272: \n273: ---\n274: \n275: ## 8. Concurrency\n276: \n277: ### File Lock Pattern\n278: \n279: ```go\n280: func (s *IndexStore) AppendEntry(entry PromptEntry) error {\n281:     lock, err := lockfile.New(s.LockPath()) // .entire/prompts/index.lock\n282:     if err != nil {\n283:         return err\n284:     }\n285:     if err := lock.TryLock(); err != nil {\n286:         return s.retryAppend(entry, 3) // max 3 attempts, 50ms backoff\n287:     }\n288:     defer lock.Unlock()\n289:     return s.appendLine(entry)\n290: }\n291: ```\n292: \n293: ### NFS Fallback\n294: \n295: Detect via `statfs`. If NFS, use `.lock` file with PID-based ownership check (same pattern as git).\n296: \n297: ---\n298: \n299: ## 9. Benchmarks\n300: \n301: | Operation | Target |\n302: |---|---|\n303: | Index load — 1K checkpoints | < 100ms |\n304: | Index load — 10K checkpoints | < 500ms |\n305: | Search — 1K checkpoints | < 20ms |\n306: | Search — 10K checkpoints | < 100ms |\n307: | Index append (new checkpoint) | < 50ms |\n308: | Full rebuild — 1K checkpoints | < 10s |\n309: \n310: ---\n311: \n312: ## 10. Testing Plan\n313: \n314: - **Unit tests:** scorer, tokenizer, tokenize/score edge cases\n315: - **Benchmark tests (`testing.B`):** `BenchmarkSearch1K`, `BenchmarkSearch10K`, `BenchmarkIndexLoad`\n316: - **Golden file tests:** CLI output formatting\n317: - **Integration tests:** temporary git repo with real checkpoint data\n318: - **Concurrent write test:** two goroutines writing simultaneously\n319: - **Edge case tests:** empty prompts, long prompts, multi-turn, unicode, special chars, corrupt index\n320: \n321: ---\n322: \n323: ## 11. Acceptance Criteria\n324: \n325: - [ ] `entire prompts search` < 100ms for 1K, < 500ms for 10K\n326: - [ ] Stemming active — \"caching\" matches \"cache\"\n327: - [ ] Multi-turn indexed per-turn with `TurnIndex`\n328: - [ ] `--json` in non-TTY emits PII warning to stderr\n329: - [ ] Concurrent writes do not corrupt index\n330: - [ ] Cold start auto-rebuild with progress bar\n331: - [ ] No new CGO dependencies\n332: - [ ] All benchmark targets met\n333: \n334: ---\n335: \n336: ## 12. New Dependencies\n337: \n338: - `github.com/kljensen/snowball` — pure Go Porter stemmer, MIT license, zero CGO\n339: \n340: ---\n341: \n342: ## 13. Integration Points\n343: \n344: 1. **PostCommit hook** (`strategy/manual_commit_hooks.go`): After `writeCommitted` succeeds, call `prompts.IndexBuilder.AppendFromCheckpoint()`\n345: 2. **`entire prompts index --rebuild`**: Walk `entire/checkpoints/v1` tree, read each session's `prompt.txt`, write fresh `index.ndjson`\n346: 3. **`entire prompts show`**: Reads from git tree (not index) — uses `checkpoint/committed.go` methods\n347: \n348: ---\n349: \n350: ## 14. Implementation Checklist\n351: \n352: - [ ] `cmd/entire/cli/prompts/index/schema.go` — types\n353: - [ ] `cmd/entire/cli/prompts/index/store.go` — read/append/lock\n354: - [ ] `cmd/entire/cli/prompts/index/rank.go` — tokenizer/stemmer/scorer\n355: - [ ] `cmd/entire/cli/prompts/index/builder.go` — walk checkpoint tree\n356: - [ ] `cmd/entire/cli/prompts/prompts.go` — command group\n357: - [ ] `cmd/entire/cli/prompts/search.go` — search command\n358: - [ ] `cmd/entire/cli/prompts/list.go` — list command\n359: - [ ] `cmd/entire/cli/prompts/show.go` — show command\n360: - [ ] `cmd/entire/cli/prompts/index_cmd.go` — index command (rebuild/status/verify)\n361: - [ ] PostCommit hook integration\n362: - [ ] Unit tests + benchmarks\n363: - [ ] `mise run check` passes\n\n(End of file - total 363 lines)\n</content>",
